WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:02.440
Begin with the inspection question.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.630
Define the asset, component, suspected condition, decision, timeframe,

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:06.720
and intended reviewer.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.945
A request to inspect a bridge is too broad;

00:00:08.945 --> 00:00:12.595
a useful objective identifies which areas and evidence are needed.

00:00:12.595 --> 00:00:16.920
Required detail determines sensor, lens, distance, angle, speed, and coverage.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.840
A broad condition survey needs context,

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.995
while a small component may need close visual evidence collected from a safe authorized

00:00:22.995 --> 00:00:23.665
standoff.

00:00:23.665 --> 00:00:25.638
Review access and safety constraints.

00:00:25.638 --> 00:00:29.550
Consider controlled areas, traffic, rail, electrical equipment, confined spaces,

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.025
emissions, moving machinery, people, wildlife, terrain, and emergency operations.

00:00:34.025 --> 00:00:37.035
The drone does not remove ground risk or site coordination.

00:00:37.035 --> 00:00:41.680
Define deliverables before flight: overview images, close-ups, video, thermal files, maps,

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.430
annotations, defect tables, or comparison products.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:48.195
Specify resolution, location context, naming, metadata, confidence,

00:00:48.195 --> 00:00:50.360
and specialist-review needs.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.960
Stakeholders should agree on what the drone can and cannot establish.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.230
A visual survey may prioritize follow-up without certifying asset condition.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:00.615
Thermal screening may identify an anomaly without diagnosing its cause.

00:01:00.615 --> 00:01:03.960
Set explicit exclusions for private areas, unrelated infrastructure,

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.664
sensitive security features, and unnecessary people.

00:01:06.664 --> 00:01:10.840
Scope controls flight time, privacy, data volume, and analytical noise.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.635
Changes should be approved rather than improvised during collection.

00:01:13.635 --> 00:01:16.250
Define acceptance criteria for the deliverable.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.125
Required components, maximum missing coverage, target pixel detail, reference views,

00:01:20.125 --> 00:01:22.641
annotation rules, turnaround,

00:01:22.641 --> 00:01:24.740
and review authority should be understood before the crew leaves the site.
